arm64: dts: rockchip: khadas-edge-v: PCIe off unless boot.scr turns it on

Khadas Edge1, Android 14 on mainline 6.12. Applied to kernel/mainline by
build/build-kernel.sh before every build (device/khadas/edge/kernel/patches/).

The M.2 slot needs the PCIe host and its PHY built in: modules are not
loaded on this board, and an Android installed on an NVMe has to find its
partitions in first-stage init. But card 20, the one build that had both
built in, never reached Android's log recorder, and the PHY's "pll relock
timeout!" with an empty slot is the part of it that runs early and that
Armbian has to patch. So the driver is in the kernel and the controller is
off in the dtb the board boots: a board with an empty slot boots exactly as
before. boot.scr sets both nodes back to "okay" for "pcie=1", "system=nvme"
or "install=nvme" in edge1-options.txt.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-khadas-edge-v.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-khadas-edge-v.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-khadas-edge-v.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-khadas-edge-v.dts
@@ -29,3 +29,17 @@ &pcie0 {
 	num-lanes = <4>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * The M.2 slot, off until asked for. The host and PHY drivers are built in
+ * for an NVMe install; card 20, which last had them built in, stopped before
+ * Android with the slot empty. boot.scr turns both back on for pcie=1,
+ * system=nvme or install=nvme in edge1-options.txt.
+ */
+&pcie_phy {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&pcie0 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
